00:17:53.281 --> 00:17:56.801
I'd love your take on
what's hard about this job

00:17:56.801 --> 00:18:00.254
and how's it changed with the pandemic?

00:18:01.235 --> 00:18:03.173
- Yeah, that's a really
interesting question.

00:18:03.173 --> 00:18:05.134
What's hard about this job?

00:18:08.591 --> 00:18:11.261
I don't wanna sound like
a Pollyanna, but honestly,

00:18:11.261 --> 00:18:13.501
this is like the funnest
job I've ever had.

00:18:13.501 --> 00:18:17.431
So I'm just gonna say
that I love what I do.

00:18:17.431 --> 00:18:19.531
I love the people that I work with.

00:18:19.531 --> 00:18:23.901
And I believe every day
I am so reinforced for me

00:18:23.901 --> 00:18:26.421
about the impact that
we're having on the world.

00:18:26.421 --> 00:18:28.031
So it's really hard to say what's hard.

00:18:28.031 --> 00:18:30.216
What's hard is that there's a lot to do.

00:18:30.216 --> 00:18:34.131
What's hard is that we are
at a stage of our growth,

00:18:34.131 --> 00:18:36.841
where we are working on a project

00:18:36.841 --> 00:18:39.491
that we have codenamed Goliath,

00:18:39.491 --> 00:18:42.311
which we have posted about in our blogs.

00:18:42.311 --> 00:18:46.121
And it's called Goliath
because we are basically moving

00:18:46.121 --> 00:18:50.181
our back end server monolith
of about 800,000 lines of code

00:18:50.181 --> 00:18:52.891
from Python two to services

00:18:54.341 --> 00:18:56.391
based architecture

00:18:56.391 --> 00:18:57.951
Written in gold.

00:18:57.951 --> 00:19:00.701
So it's big and it's going into go.

00:19:00.701 --> 00:19:03.141
So Goliath is hard.

00:19:03.141 --> 00:19:07.161
We have a fantastic team
who's doing a great job on it.

00:19:07.161 --> 00:19:10.004
But it is a hard, hard thing to do.

00:19:11.471 --> 00:19:13.191
As one of my leaders on the team

00:19:13.191 --> 00:19:15.201
that manages the platform says,

00:19:15.201 --> 00:19:18.501
it's like, we're still flying the plane.

00:19:18.501 --> 00:19:20.171
And it's kind of all in pieces,

00:19:20.171 --> 00:19:23.481
but we're still keeping all
the passengers on the plane

00:19:23.481 --> 00:19:24.704
and flying the plane.

00:19:25.611 --> 00:19:29.381
Or I say, it's kind of like
switching out the foundation

00:19:29.381 --> 00:19:32.301
in from under your house,
the entire foundation

00:19:32.301 --> 00:19:33.951
while you're living in the house.

00:19:35.301 --> 00:19:36.600
- Well, there's a party in the house

00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:37.614
- And using all the functions.

00:19:39.181 --> 00:19:41.941
Well, there's a party in
the house and a pandemic,

00:19:41.941 --> 00:19:44.344
by the way, so everybodyis in the house

00:19:44.344 --> 00:19:45.464
all the time.

00:19:50.345 --> 00:19:53.031
- I know exactly, I mean, I
you know, just to add to that,

00:19:53.031 --> 00:19:57.051
I think one of the things
that I found difficult

00:19:57.051 --> 00:19:59.721
